And just like that, your request will take advantage of any established connections to that
same external resource. If there are no other requests associated with the specified
ConnectionGroupName property, then .NET Core will create a connection in its connection
pool, and associate your request as the first in the connection group. This is especially
useful if a set of requests are targeting a resource that requires access credentials, as the
connection is established with those access credentials once, and then shared with the
subsequent requests!
